    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, thanks. Quick follow up though—if we had a partial year where we bought the machine halfway through the fiscal year, how would that change the math for the first year's entry?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a partial year, you simply need to prorate the annual depreciation expense based on the number of months the equipment was in use during that fiscal year. If you bought the machine halfway through the year, you would use six months instead of the full twelve. So, you would take your full annual depreciation of $12,500 and multiply it by the fraction of the year the machine was operational, which is 6/12 or 0.5. This would result in a first-year depreciation expense of $6,250.",
      "source": "target",
